---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DesignTodo from './DesignTodo.astro';
import '../styles/firstchoice.css';
import '../styles/firstchoice-2026.css';
const { locale = 'en' } = Astro.props;
const es = locale === 'es';
const root = es ? '/es/' : '/';
const professions = ['Nursing','Engineering','Electrician','Insurance','Cosmetology'];
const capabilities = ['Product Strategy','Information Architecture','UX / UI','E-commerce','Learning Experience','Design Systems','Service Design','Responsive Design'];
const requirements = [['STATE','Florida'],['PROFESSION','Registered Nurse'],['CREDIT HOURS','24 hours'],['RENEWAL DATE','May 31, 2027']];
---
<BaseLayout locale={locale} title="1st Choice CE — Continuing education without the administrative friction" description="A retrospective product exploration for professional continuing education and license compliance.">
<article class="fc">
  <header class="fc-hero fc-wrap"><a class="fc-back" href={`${root}#projects`}>← {es?'Todos los proyectos':'All projects'}</a><div class="fc-top"><span>1ST CHOICE CE / CONTINUING EDUCATION</span><span>UNITED STATES / 2026</span></div><h1>Continuing education<br/><em>without the administrative friction.</em></h1><div class="fc-intro"><p>Professional continuing education is rarely a simple content problem. Students need to identify the right requirement, find an approved course for their profession and state, complete it on time, receive documentation and understand what happens next.</p><p>1st Choice CE turns that process into a digital service. This retrospective case study revisits my previous work around the platform and explores how its brand and product experience could operate today as one connected system.</p></div><span class="fc-badge">Retrospective product exploration</span></header>

  <div class="fc-ecosystem fc-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí hero ecosystem — Course Finder, Course Detail, Dashboard, Certificate y mobile progress"/><div class="finder-mini"><header><b>1ST CHOICE / CE</b><span>COURSE FINDER</span></header><small>FIND THE RIGHT COURSE FOR YOUR LICENSE</small><h2>Start with your<br/>profession and state.</h2><div><label>PROFESSION<strong>Registered Nurse</strong></label><label>STATE<strong>Florida</strong></label></div><button>Show my requirements →</button></div><div class="course-mini"><span>BOARD APPROVED</span><small>FLORIDA / NURSING</small><h3>Prevention of Medical Errors</h3><dl><div><dt>Credit</dt><dd>2 CE hours</dd></div><div><dt>Format</dt><dd>Online / self-paced</dd></div></dl><b>$18.00</b></div><div class="phone-mini"><small>YOUR RENEWAL</small><strong>18 / 24</strong><span>HOURS COMPLETE</span><i></i><b>Patient Safety</b><small>60% COMPLETE</small></div><div class="cert-mini"><small>CERTIFICATE OF COMPLETION</small><b>Maria Rodriguez</b><span>Professional Ethics / 3 CE Hours</span></div></div>

  <section class="fc-section fc-wrap"><span class="fc-num">01</span><div><small>01 / CONTEXT</small><h2>The student is not looking for a course.<br/><em>They are trying to renew a license.</em></h2><p>Continuing education sits at the intersection of learning and administration. An electrician, nurse, insurance agent or engineer may arrive with a different profession, different state rules and different renewal requirements, but the underlying question is remarkably consistent: What exactly do I need to complete?</p><p>The experience must help users move from regulatory uncertainty to a clear, purchasable path.</p></div></section>
  <div class="compliance-path fc-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí secuencia license → requirement → course → completion → certificate → reporting → renewal"/>{['LICENSE','REQUIREMENT','COURSE','COMPLETION','CERTIFICATE','REPORTING','RENEWAL'].map((x,i)=><div><span>0{i+1}</span><b>{x}</b>{i<6&&<i>→</i>}</div>)}</div>
  <blockquote class="fc-callout fc-wrap"><span>FROM / “I need continuing education.”</span><strong>“This is the course I need.<br/>It is approved. I can finish it here.<br/>I know what happens after completion.”</strong></blockquote>

  <section class="fc-section fc-wrap"><span class="fc-num">02</span><div><small>02 / INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE</small><h2>One catalog. Hundreds of different entry points.</h2><p>Courses differ by state, profession, duration, approval authority, regulatory topic and renewal requirement. The information architecture therefore needs to answer two questions immediately: who are you, and where are you licensed? Only then does the catalog become useful.</p></div></section>
  <div class="matrix fc-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí mapa State × Profession × Requirement"/><div><small>01 / WHERE ARE YOU LICENSED?</small>{['Texas','Florida','Illinois','Arizona','California'].map((x,i)=><button class:list={{active:i===1}}>{x}<span>{i===1?'SELECTED':'→'}</span></button>)}</div><b>×</b><div><small>02 / WHAT IS YOUR PROFESSION?</small>{['Insurance','Nursing','Electrician','Engineering','Cosmetology'].map((x,i)=><button class:list={{active:i===1}}>{x}<span>{i===1?'SELECTED':'→'}</span></button>)}</div><aside><small>RESULT</small><strong>Florida / Registered Nurse</strong><span>24 CE hours required</span><span>11 approved courses</span></aside></div>

  <section class="fc-section fc-wrap"><span class="fc-num">03</span><div><small>03 / COURSE FINDER</small><h2>Ask for the minimum. Return what matters.</h2><p>A useful course finder should not feel like a regulatory form. Two confident choices — profession and state — can convert an unstructured catalog into a relevant set of approved options.</p></div></section>
  <figure class="fc-asset fc-wide"><img src="/projects/okhosting/2026/1st-choice/f6200621-31e0-4c8f-8e47-cb7c7a1e6474.webp" alt="1st Choice CE course finder for Registered Nurse in Florida" loading="lazy"/><figcaption><span>COURSE FINDER</span><b>Profession → state → approved renewal results.</b></figcaption></figure>

  <section class="fc-section fc-wrap"><span class="fc-num">04</span><div><small>04 / COURSE DETAIL</small><h2>Make approval visible before persuasion.</h2><p>A course detail page needs to work as commerce, compliance record and learning overview at once. Approval, hours, state, profession, format, certificate and reporting should be clear before the user reaches price.</p></div></section>
  <div class="course-detail fc-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí Course Detail"/><div class="cd-main"><div class="cd-tags"><span>BOARD APPROVED</span><span>FLORIDA</span><span>NURSING</span></div><small>COURSE / 001-CE</small><h2>Prevention of<br/>Medical Errors</h2><p>Required continuing education for Florida Registered Nurses and Licensed Practical Nurses.</p><div class="cd-facts">{[['CREDIT HOURS','2 CE'],['FORMAT','Online / self-paced'],['CERTIFICATE','Instant'],['REPORTING','Where applicable']].map(([a,b])=><div><small>{a}</small><b>{b}</b></div>)}</div><h3>What this course covers</h3><ul><li>Root-cause analysis and error prevention</li><li>Patient safety standards</li><li>Florida reporting requirements</li></ul></div><aside><small>APPROVAL</small><strong>Florida Board of Nursing</strong><span>Provider no. 0010781</span><hr/><small>PRICE</small><b>$18.00</b><button>Start course →</button><a>Add to renewal plan</a></aside></div>

  <section class="fc-section fc-wrap"><span class="fc-num">05</span><div><small>05 / COMMERCE</small><h2>Sell the requirement, not twelve separate courses.</h2><p>When a license renewal requires several topics or credit hours, purchasing individual courses becomes another administrative task. Bundles can package the requirement as a complete path: this is what you need for your renewal.</p></div></section>
  <figure class="fc-asset fc-wide"><img src="/projects/okhosting/2026/1st-choice/f720a256-06cc-4c3c-ae35-9193bd6681c0.webp" alt="Florida RN LPN complete renewal package" loading="lazy"/><figcaption><span>RENEWAL PACKAGE</span><b>24 hours · 11 courses · 100% requirement coverage.</b></figcaption></figure>

  <section class="fc-section fc-wrap"><span class="fc-num">06</span><div><small>06 / CHECKOUT</small><h2>A short path from requirement to enrollment.</h2><p>Once the correct course has been identified, checkout should introduce as little additional uncertainty as possible. The order summary repeats the critical information and what happens after completion.</p></div></section>
  <figure class="fc-asset fc-wide"><img src="/projects/okhosting/2026/1st-choice/abf448f3-535b-4564-b294-e941bc91c353.webp" alt="1st Choice CE checkout on desktop and mobile" loading="lazy"/><figcaption><span>CHECKOUT 2026</span><b>Course, account, payment and a regulatory summary — on desktop and mobile.</b></figcaption></figure>

  <section class="fc-section fc-wrap"><span class="fc-num">07</span><div><small>07 / LEARNING PRODUCT</small><h2>Get in. Learn. Finish.</h2><p>Once enrolled, discovery disappears and progress becomes the primary interaction. Students should always understand where they are, how much remains, what action comes next and what is required for completion.</p></div></section>
  <figure class="fc-asset fc-wide"><img src="/projects/okhosting/2026/1st-choice/5098ae0f-5722-471d-8374-97e7c2ced7c5.webp" alt="1st Choice CE course player with lesson progress and ethical scenario" loading="lazy"/><figcaption><span>COURSE PLAYER</span><b>Lesson flow, scenario question, progress and save &amp; exit.</b></figcaption></figure>

  <section class="fc-section fc-wrap"><span class="fc-num">08</span><div><small>08 / STUDENT EXPERIENCE</small><h2>Everything needed for renewal in one place.</h2><p>After purchase, the account area becomes the student's home for active courses, completed credits, certificates and reporting status. The system can turn a series of transactions into a clear renewal record.</p><span class="fc-badge">Conceptual product extension</span></div></section>
  <figure class="fc-asset fc-wide"><img src="/projects/okhosting/2026/1st-choice/cb89dc14-6027-46b8-911b-558d517c3c30.webp" alt="Student dashboard with Florida RN renewal progress" loading="lazy"/><figcaption><span>STUDENT DASHBOARD</span><b>18 / 24 hours, active learning, certificates and reporting status in one place.</b></figcaption></figure>

  <section class="fc-section fc-wrap"><span class="fc-num">09</span><div><small>09 / COMPLETION</small><h2>Finishing the course should feel definitive.</h2><p>For a regulated profession, the student needs proof. The completion state connects the educational milestone to the administrative one through certificate access, credit information and reporting status.</p></div></section>
  <figure class="fc-asset fc-wide"><img src="/projects/okhosting/2026/1st-choice/1953eaa0-1220-43d2-817b-63357806c2ad.webp" alt="Course completion screen and large certificate of completion" loading="lazy"/><figcaption><span>COMPLETION + CERTIFICATE</span><b>Earned credit, certificate ready and reporting status — paired with the document itself.</b></figcaption></figure>

  <section class="fc-section fc-wrap"><span class="fc-num">10</span><div><small>10 / DOCUMENT SYSTEM</small><h2>A certificate is a product artifact.</h2><p>Certificates may enter employer records, appear in audits or remain stored for years. They require their own document logic: strong hierarchy, verification information and enough restraint to remain legible in print and digital form.</p></div></section>
  <div class="certificate-spec fc-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí sistema completo de Certificate — print, detail y mobile"/><div class="cert-large"><small>1ST CHOICE CONTINUING EDUCATION</small><h2>CERTIFICATE<br/><em>OF COMPLETION</em></h2><p>STUDENT</p><strong>Maria Rodriguez</strong><div>{[['COURSE','Professional Ethics'],['CREDIT','3 CE Hours'],['COMPLETION','August 18, 2026'],['CERTIFICATE ID','1CE-28390']].map(([a,b])=><span><small>{a}</small><b>{b}</b></span>)}</div><footer><i>1ST<br/>CE</i><span>Authorized Provider<br/>Provider no. 0010781</span><b>VERIFY ↗</b></footer></div><aside><small>VERIFICATION RECORD</small><div class="qr">1CE<br/>28390</div><p>Certificate ID<br/><b>1CE-28390</b></p><p>Status<br/><b>VALID / VERIFIED</b></p></aside></div>

  <section class="fc-section fc-wrap"><span class="fc-num">11</span><div><small>11 / SERVICE COMMUNICATION</small><h2>Tell students exactly what happens next.</h2><p>Purchase confirmation, course completion, certificate delivery and reporting updates should remove uncertainty rather than merely confirm that an email was sent.</p></div></section>
  <div class="fc-emails fc-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí emails de enrollment, completion y reporting"/>{[['YOU’RE ENROLLED','Florida Nursing Renewal Package','START COURSE'],['COURSE COMPLETE','Your certificate is ready.','DOWNLOAD CERTIFICATE'],['COMPLETION REPORTED','Credits: 2 hours · Aug 18, 2026','VIEW RECORD']].map(([a,b,c],i)=><article><header><b>1ST CHOICE / CE</b><span>0{i+1}</span></header><small>SERVICE UPDATE</small><h3>{a}</h3><p>{b}</p><div><span>STATUS</span><b>{i===0?'READY TO START':i===1?'CERTIFICATE READY':'BOARD SUBMITTED'}</b></div><button>{c} →</button></article>)}</div>

  <section class="fc-section fc-wrap"><span class="fc-num">12</span><div><small>12 / RESPONSIVE EXPERIENCE</small><h2>Professional education happens between everything else.</h2><p>Course discovery, purchase, reading, progress and certificate access all need usable mobile states. Mobile cannot be treated as a compressed desktop layout.</p></div></section>
  <figure class="fc-asset fc-wide"><img src="/projects/okhosting/2026/1st-choice/dc3c2c7d-c2f5-4dd1-9856-4801aab68250.webp" alt="Four responsive 1st Choice CE mobile views" loading="lazy"/><figcaption><span>RESPONSIVE SEQUENCE</span><b>Finder, course detail, continue learning and certificate ready as native mobile moments.</b></figcaption></figure>

  <section class="fc-section fc-wrap"><span class="fc-num">13</span><div><small>13 / DESIGN SYSTEM</small><h2>One language across hundreds of courses.</h2><p>State, profession, hours, approval status, packages, pricing and course progress appear repeatedly throughout the product. Encoding those patterns into reusable components allows the platform to grow without redesigning every new course manually.</p></div></section>
  <div class="fc-system fc-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí design system board con componentes nacidos del producto"/><header><span>1CE / PRODUCT SYSTEM</span><b>CORE COMPONENTS / 01—15</b></header><div class="sys-grid"><div class="badges"><span>BOARD APPROVED</span><span>2 CE HOURS</span><span>FLORIDA</span><span>NURSING</span></div><article><small>FLORIDA / NURSING</small><h3>Patient Safety</h3><p>2 CE hours · Self-paced</p><b>BOARD APPROVED</b></article><div class="statuses">{['ACTIVE','COMPLETE','REPORTED','PROCESSING'].map(x=><span><i></i>{x}</span>)}</div><div class="progresses">{['0%','37%','100%'].map((x,i)=><div><span>{x}</span><i><b style={`width:${i===0?0:i===1?37:100}%`}></b></i></div>)}</div><label>STATE<select><option>Florida</option></select></label><button>Start course →</button></div></div>

  <section class="fc-section fc-wrap"><span class="fc-num">14</span><div><small>14 / VISUAL LANGUAGE</small><h2>Authority without institutional distance.</h2><p>Deep blue anchors the system in trust and documentation. Lighter blue distinguishes interactive and educational layers. A warm neutral prevents the interface from becoming visually clinical.</p></div></section>
  <div class="brand-sheet fc-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí brand sheet — typography, color, taxonomy, imagery y UI patterns"/><div class="type"><small>DISPLAY / INTERFACE</small><strong>Aa</strong><h3>Clear enough<br/>to act on.</h3></div><div class="fc-colors"><span>#153D5A</span><span>#B9DFFF</span><span>#F1EEE6</span></div><div class="taxonomy">{professions.map((x,i)=><span><i>0{i+1}</i>{x}</span>)}</div></div>

  <section class="fc-section fc-wrap"><span class="fc-num">15</span><div><small>15 / CONTENT SYSTEM</small><h2>Many professions. One recognizable platform.</h2><p>A secondary taxonomy can distinguish professions through controlled color, iconography and imagery while preserving the core 1st Choice CE system.</p></div></section>
  <div class="profession-grid fc-wide">{professions.map((x,i)=><article class={`prof-${i}`}><small>PROFESSION / 0{i+1}</small><h3>{x}</h3><p>{['Patient care, safety and mandatory topics.','Ethics, standards and technical responsibility.','Codes, safety and state renewal.','Licensing, ethics and product requirements.','Health, sanitation and professional practice.'][i]}</p><span>View {x} courses →</span></article>)}</div>

  <section class="fc-section fc-wrap"><span class="fc-num">16</span><div><small>16 / B2B EXTENSION</small><span class="fc-badge">Conceptual product extension</span><h2>Compliance at team scale.</h2><p>A manager may need visibility across dozens of employees, professions, completion dates and certificates. A lightweight employer environment extends the consumer product into workforce compliance.</p></div></section>
  <figure class="fc-asset fc-wide"><img src="/projects/okhosting/2026/1st-choice/a4e8a86e-f9cc-4da3-a084-d1975bafc0f5.webp" alt="Employer dashboard for team continuing education compliance" loading="lazy"/><figcaption><span>EMPLOYER DASHBOARD</span><b>46 employees, compliance signals, training assignment and exportable records.</b></figcaption></figure>

  <section class="fc-section fc-wrap"><span class="fc-num">17</span><div><small>17 / OPERATIONS</small><span class="fc-badge">Conceptual product extension</span><h2>A catalog this large needs an operational system behind it.</h2><p>Courses carry state-specific approval information, provider numbers, prices, renewal requirements and reporting rules. An internal interface can make those relationships explicit instead of burying them inside generic CMS fields.</p></div></section>
  <div class="admin-editor fc-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí Admin Course Editor"/><header><b>COURSE OPERATIONS</b><span>DRAFT SAVED / 14:32</span><button>Publish changes</button></header><div><nav><span>01 Course</span><span>02 Requirements</span><span>03 Certificate</span><span>04 Reporting</span><span>05 Commerce</span></nav><main><small>COURSE RECORD / 001-CE</small><h2>Engineering Ethics</h2><div class="admin-fields">{[['PROFESSION','Engineering'],['STATE','Florida'],['CREDIT HOURS','1'],['BOARD','Florida Board of Professional Engineers'],['PROVIDER NUMBER','0010781'],['APPROVAL STATUS','ACTIVE'],['CERTIFICATE','Enabled'],['REPORTING','Within 24 hours'],['PRICE','$14.00']].map(([a,b])=><label><span>{a}</span><b>{b}</b></label>)}</div></main></div></div>

  <section class="fc-archive"><div class="fc-wrap archive-copy"><div><small>18 / ORIGINAL ARCHIVE</small><h2>Where the project began.</h2></div><p>My original work with 1st Choice CE belongs to an earlier phase of both the platform and my own practice. The material below comes from that professional archive. The product system shown throughout the case study is a contemporary retrospective exploration based on that foundation.</p></div><div class="archive-label fc-wrap"><b>ORIGINAL PROFESSIONAL WORK</b><span>SEPARATE FROM</span><b>2026 RETROSPECTIVE PRODUCT EXPLORATION</b></div><div class="fc-archive-grid fc-wide"><img src="/projects/firstchoice/1ST-CHOICE.jpg" alt="Original 1st Choice CE professional work"/><img src="/projects/firstchoice/1ST-CHOICE-2048x1177.jpg" alt="Original 1st Choice CE website archive"/><img src="/projects/firstchoice/1st-2.png" alt="Original 1st Choice CE identity archive"/></div></section>

  <section class="fc-reflection fc-wrap"><span class="fc-num">19</span><div><small>19 / REFLECTION</small><h2>Designing the course is only part of designing the service.</h2><p>The student experience begins before enrollment, with uncertainty about requirements, and continues after completion through certificates, reporting and license renewal. The opportunity is larger than creating attractive course pages. It is about designing a clear path through a regulated process.</p><div>{capabilities.map(x=><span>{x}</span>)}</div><small>Original professional work + 2026 retrospective conceptual development.</small></div></section>
  <div class="fc-final fc-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí final ecosystem image"/><small>ONE SERVICE / EVERY STEP</small><h2>FIND.<br/>LEARN.<br/><em>COMPLETE.</em></h2><div><span>COURSE APPROVED</span><span>CERTIFICATE READY</span><span>COMPLETION REPORTED</span></div></div>
  <a class="fc-next fc-wrap" href={`${root}project/caintra/`}><span>NEXT PROJECT</span><strong>Caintra</strong><b>↗</b></a>
</article>
</BaseLayout>
